ce department and  we've seen historically low levels of  crime uh just a couple years ago we had  the lowest homicide rate since 1954. and  then the last thing is we're focusing on  quality of life because one of the  things i've learned i'm 43 years old in  my life is the one commodity you can't  get back you can't trade you can't get  more of it's time and so  you know we invest and we do all these  things so we can have the ability to do  what we want with our time and so if you  design a city around that fact  and you focus on you know cultural  facilities of which we continue to  invest in if you focus on parks we just  did a 100 million dollar linear park  called the underlying you focus on  sports uh we have uh all the major  sports plus formula one that's beginning  next year they just did a 10-year deal  where the only the second city in  america has formula one and we're the  only city that has all the sports and  formula one probably in the world  and then you talk about homelessness  which is another quality of life issue  we have 510 homeless in our city we're  at the lowest level since 2013  and we just got passed through our  dollars or what i call a functional  homeless plan which is to hopefully be  one of the first big cities in america  uh to to reduce homelessness to zero so  that is is is sort of the  the importance of local government how  it touches on all of those aspects of  your life your quality of life and i  think uh you know i think that is  important for people to realize federal  government is obviously your federal tax  dollars your income tax and how that's  spent on national security uh as social  security and welfare uh or things of  that nature um you know social programs  uh and and your state is mostly a state  income tax which is a consumption tax um  but the city are the ones that pick up  your garbage they police your streets  and and they keep you safe and protected  hey guys bang bang thanks so much for  watching the best